  "correct": "2",
  "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/ebadc30a979bf1a7e953d20901c3e7953c575296c0e0bb4af8a458ec3a64ab2c.png] \n\nGiven statement : 3 × 7 − 5 + 2 = 10 \n\nAccording to the question, after interchanging the two numbers :\n\nSo,\n\n__\n \n• Option - (1) : 10 and 7 \n\n3 × 7 − 5 + 2 = 10 ⇒ **3 × 10**__ − 5 + 2 = 7\n\n__**30 + 2**__ - 5 = 7\n\n__**32 - 5**__ = 7\n\n27 ≠ 7 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n__\n \n• Option - (2) : 7 and 5 \n\n3 × 7 − 5 + 2 = 10 ⇒ **3 × 5**__ − 7 + 2 = 10\n\n__**15 + 2**__ - 7 = 10\n\n__**17 - 7**__ = 10\n\n**10 = 10 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n__\n \n• Option - (3) : 3 and 5\n\n3 × 7 − 5 + 2 = 10 ⇒ **5**____** × 7**__ − 3 + 2 = 10\n\n__**12 + 2**__ - 3 = 10\n\n__**14 - 3**__ = 10\n\n11 ≠ 10 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n__\n \n• Option - (4) : 3 and 2 \n\n3 × 7 − 5 + 2 = 10 ⇒ **2**____** × 7**__ − 5 + 3 = 10\n\n__**14 + 3**__ - 5 = 10\n\n__**17 - 5**__ = 10\n\n12 ≠ 10 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, \"Option - (2)\" is the correct answer.",
